=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/freeze_all_enemies.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "freeze_all_enemies",
        display_name: "Freeze All Enemies",
        tagline: Some(
            "Time stops for goons. You don't.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Every freeze tick (200 ms), walks GUObjectArray for every live Character instance and writes 0.0001 to AActor::CustomTimeDilation (engine-level offset +0x68). UE5 multiplies world delta-time by an actor's CustomTimeDilation each tick — at 0.0001 that's a ~10000x slowdown, effectively a stop. Animations, AI decisions, melee-swing windups, and projectile spawns all halt for affected actors. Filters exclude the player (`_Playable_`), vehicles (`_VEH_`), class defaults (`Default__`), engine transients (`/Engine/Transient/`), and crowd NPCs (`BP_Population_`), so only combat-engageable enemies (goons, lieutenants, bosses) are frozen. Combine with Infinite Health for a no-risk demolition derby, or with One-Hit Kill to walk the room and tap each enemy. Toggle OFF restores each frozen enemy's original CustomTimeDilation (usually 1.0) from a per-instance snapshot — frozen enemies unfreeze within ~one tick. Newly-spawned enemies after the toggle is OFF were never touched.",
        ),
        icon: Some(
            "snowflake",
        ),
        icon_color: None,
        tier: "combat",
        kind: "mod",
        discovered_in_version: Some(
            "1.0.0.1",
        ),
        verified_versions: [
            "1.0.0.1",
        ],
        discovered_on: Some(
            "2026-05-25",
        ),
        discovered_by: None,
    },
    value: None,
    write: FreezeForMatching {
        class_path: "",
        class_name_substrings: [
            "_Goon_C",
            "_SWAT_",
            "Arkham",
            "TwoFace",
        ],
        field_offsets: [
            104,
        ],
        value: Some(
            0.0001,
        ),
        value_bytes: None,
        interval_ms: 200,
        max_results: 2048,
        include_fqn_contains: [],
        exclude_fqn_contains: [
            "_Playable_",
            "_VEH_",
            "Default__",
            "/Engine/Transient/",
            "BP_Population_",
        ],
    },
    locator: None,
    heap_scan: None,
    reflection: None,
    pointer_chain: None,
    control: Some(
        Switch,
    ),
}

=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/goons_ignore_you.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "goons_ignore_you",
        display_name: "Goons Ignore You",
        tagline: Some(
            "You walk through Gotham's worst. They can't see you as a threat anymore.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Every freeze tick (250 ms), iterates every live combatant Character (goons, GCPD SWAT, Arkham inmates, Two-Face crew) and stamps the **player's CurrentTeamTag** (FGameplayTag at +0xB28, 8 bytes) onto each one. With the same team tag as the player, UE5's combat-attitude resolution returns Friendly → enemies treat you as an ally and ignore you entirely. Walk past patrols, sneak through encounters, traverse hub zones without aggro pulls. Caveats: (1) **Friends can't be attacked back** — TT's framework refuses your hits on same-team actors. This is a peace mode, not a one-sided slaughter mode. Toggle OFF before engaging if you want to fight. (2) Toggle OFF restores each stamped goon's original team tag from a per-instance snapshot taken on the first write — goons currently in your area go back to hostile within ~one tick. Newly-spawned goons after the toggle is OFF were never touched. (3) Player tag value (`20 69 B3 00 00 00 00 00`) is verified against build 1.0.0.1 — likely shifts on future builds. (4) Allied factions (Robin / Nightwing / GCPD allies) are unaffected since they're excluded by `_Playable_` and the player-tag stamp matches what they already had.",
        ),
        icon: Some(
            "shield-off",
        ),
        icon_color: None,
        tier: "world",
        kind: "mod",
        discovered_in_version: Some(
            "1.0.0.1",
        ),
        verified_versions: [
            "1.0.0.1",
        ],
        discovered_on: Some(
            "2026-05-25",
        ),
        discovered_by: None,
    },
    value: None,
    write: FreezeForMatching {
        class_path: "",
        class_name_substrings: [
            "_Goon_C",
            "_SWAT_",
            "Arkham",
            "TwoFace",
        ],
        field_offsets: [
            2856,
        ],
        value: None,
        value_bytes: Some(
            "20 69 B3 00 00 00 00 00",
        ),
        interval_ms: 250,
        max_results: 2048,
        include_fqn_contains: [],
        exclude_fqn_contains: [
            "_Playable_",
            "_VEH_",
            "Default__",
            "/Engine/Transient/",
        ],
    },
    locator: None,
    heap_scan: None,
    reflection: None,
    pointer_chain: None,
    control: Some(
        Switch,
    ),
}

=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/lock_health.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "lock_health",
        display_name: "Infinite Health",
        tagline: Some(
            "The Dark Knight doesn't bleed. Damage flashes, then vanishes.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "GAS-aware freeze: resolves PlayerState→PawnPrivate→HealthAttributeSet→Health (FGameplayAttributeData), then freezes Health.CurrentValue at 9999 every 100 ms. The struct's inner layout is `{ vptr(+0); BaseValue f32(+8); CurrentValue f32(+12) }`, so the chain's final hop carries `inner_offset = 12` to land on CurrentValue. UE5's GameplayAbilitySystem applies damage by mutating CurrentValue via PreAttributeChange/PostGameplayEffectExecute hooks — our 100 ms write-back races those and wins (any hit briefly drops the bar, then we restore). PreAttributeChange may clamp the freeze value to MaxHealth on entry; that's fine, the player still reads as full. This path avoids the FPV/cursor-lock bug the previous `bCanBeDamaged` approach hit — TT's framework couples bCanBeDamaged to cinematic-camera state.",
        ),
        icon: Some(
            "heart",
        ),
        icon_color: None,
        tier: "combat",
        kind: "trainer",
        discovered_in_version: Some(
            "1.0.0.1",
        ),
        verified_versions: [
            "1.0.0.1",
        ],
        discovered_on: Some(
            "2026-05-25",
        ),
        discovered_by: None,
    },
    value: Some(
        ValueSpec {
            kind: F32,
            min: Some(
                0.0,
            ),
            max: Some(
                9999.0,
            ),
            display: "decimal",
            endian: Little,
        },
    ),
    write: Freeze {
        interval_ms: 100,
        freeze_value: Some(
            9999.0,
        ),
        freeze_copy_offset: None,
    },
    locator: None,
    heap_scan: None,
    reflection: Some(
        ReflectionSpec {
            class_path: "BP_DinnerPlayerState_C",
            predicate: Contains(
                "/PersistentLevel/",
            ),
            property_name: "PawnPrivate",
            also_write: [],
            deref: [
                ReflectionDerefSpec {
                    property_name: "HealthAttributeSet",
                    inner_offset: 0,
                },
                ReflectionDerefSpec {
                    property_name: "Health",
                    inner_offset: 12,
                },
            ],
            offset: None,
        },
    ),
    pointer_chain: None,
    control: Some(
        Switch,
    ),
}

=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/mod_demolition_derby.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "mod_demolition_derby",
        display_name: "Demolition Derby",
        tagline: Some(
            "Pick how rude the taxis are today.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Freezes MassTrafficSettings.TurnSpeedScale plus the four variance fields (SpeedLimit, Speed, Acceleration, Deceleration) at the value you pick. Stock is roughly 0.5 / 0.1–0.35 across these, so even the gentle preset is noticeably chaotic. The same scalar is mirrored to all five fields via reflection `also_write` — one selection, five fields kept in sync every 200 ms. Picking 'Joker's Holiday' tends to be too extreme (cars crash and despawn faster than they spawn, so streets look emptier); 'Pile-Up Special' is the sweet spot.",
        ),
        icon: Some(
            "gi-speedometer",
        ),
        icon_color: None,
        tier: "world",
        kind: "mod",
        discovered_in_version: Some(
            "1.0.0.1",
        ),
        verified_versions: [
            "1.0.0.1",
        ],
        discovered_on: Some(
            "2026-05-25",
        ),
        discovered_by: None,
    },
    value: Some(
        ValueSpec {
            kind: F32,
            min: Some(
                0.0,
            ),
            max: Some(
                5.0,
            ),
            display: "decimal",
            endian: Little,
        },
    ),
    write: Freeze {
        interval_ms: 200,
        freeze_value: None,
        freeze_copy_offset: None,
    },
    locator: None,
    heap_scan: None,
    reflection: Some(
        ReflectionSpec {
            class_path: "MassTrafficSettings",
            predicate: FqnPrefix(
                "/Script/MassTraffic/Default__MassTrafficSettings",
            ),
            property_name: "TurnSpeedScale",
            also_write: [
                "SpeedLimitVariancePct",
                "SpeedVariancePct",
                "AccelerationVariancePct",
                "DecelerationVariancePct",
            ],
            deref: [],
            offset: None,
        },
    ),
    pointer_chain: None,
    control: Some(
        Input {
            presets: [
                Labeled {
                    label: "Tipsy Taxis",
                    value: 0.6,
                },
                Labeled {
                    label: "Pile-Up Special",
                    value: 1.0,
                },
                Labeled {
                    label: "Joker's Holiday",
                    value: 2.0,
                },
            ],
            step: None,
        },
    ),
}

