=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/stud_multiplier.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "stud_multiplier",
        display_name: "Stud Multiplier",
        tagline: Some(
            "Every pickup scaled. Pick your greed.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Pegs the TT Collectables stud-multiplier system at a user-chosen scalar. Writes the chosen value to both `StudMultiplierMin` (+0x38) and `StudMultiplierMax` (+0x3C) on the `TtCollectablesSettings` developer-settings singleton (FQN `/Script/TtCollectables/Default__TtCollectablesSettings`). The collectables subsystem reads Min as the floor and Max as the ceiling for the per-encounter multiplier; setting both equal pins the multiplier to that value for the rest of the session. Default decay/increment behavior becomes irrelevant when Min == Max. Applies immediately on click — no freeze loop needed because the settings CDO is the live source the runtime reads from. Persists across level loads. Caveats: (1) does NOT retroactively scale already-collected studs; only future pickups. (2) Some scripted-event studs (e.g. cinematic-burst piles) award fixed amounts that bypass the multiplier — those won't scale. (3) If the game has hub-vs-mission multiplier differences, both are flattened to your value while applied. To revert, reapply with value 1.0 (the vanilla floor).",
