=== SIGNATURE batman-lod/signatures/unlock_all_fast_travel.toml ===
SignatureSpec {
    meta: Meta {
        feature: "unlock_all_fast_travel",
        display_name: "Unlock All Fast Travel",
        tagline: Some(
            "Every terminal in Gotham, ready. No more rooftop sprints to the next mission.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Iterates the live PROG_FastTravelUnlock definition set (TtGameProgressDefinitionSet, one tag per fast-travel terminal in the game world) and calls TtGameProgressStatics::SetGameProgressValue(tag, 2) for each. Value 2 = unlocked on this build — same convention as skills. After firing, every fast-travel terminal across Gotham + sub-areas (Batcave, GVRP, CA01, OG01/02/03, EEAM, TC01, CAAC, NT01, etc.) is selectable from the map without needing to discover/activate it in-world. Achievements that gate on terminal-unlock state fire as a side effect. Caveats: (1) does not move the player — you still pick a destination on the map. (2) some narrative-gated terminals (e.g. locations behind story-mission walls) may still refuse travel if a parallel story-flag check fires; if that happens, advance the story past that mission and the terminal becomes usable. (3) discovery of new terminals added by post-release DLC is handled by the same system but only for terminals registered in PROG_FastTravelUnlock at the time the asset loads.",
        ),
        icon: Some(
            "map-pin",
        ),
        icon_color: None,
        tier: "progression",
        kind: "trainer",
        discovered_in_version: Some(
            "1.0.0.1",
