        feature: "game_speed",
        display_name: "Game Speed",
        tagline: Some(
            "Slow-mo or fast-forward the whole game.",
        ),
        description: Some(
            "Scales the global gameplay clock by writing the `ZGameTimeManager` singleton's `m_fGameTimeMultiplier` (f32 @ +0x68): 1.0 = normal, <1 = slow-mo, >1 = fast-forward. Pure Denuvo-safe data write — no `.text` patch. The singleton is a module static, so it is re-found each session by a structural [heap_scan] fingerprint on its vtable rather than a hardcoded address. The multiplier is not re-stamped by the engine, so a one-shot write holds; pick a preset or type a value and Apply. NOTE (per-build): the vtable `value` below is a module address — stable across launches of this build (no ASLR) but it shifts on a game update; re-derive it via RTTI (`.?AVZGameTimeManager@@`) if the feature stops resolving after a patch.\n",
